        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-manner-de-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Describe how well someone acts",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Place unstressed 得 after the action and follow it with a description. An expressed object does not go between 得 and the description: repeat the verb, or make the object the topic before the verb.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "他说得很快。",
                "pinyin": "tā shuō de hěn kuài 。",
                "meaning": "He speaks quickly.",
                "audio": "c0fe47a9a4b215e5b46ced6fe8a0ca4ecd711643057abf0610050247ec6ecd35"
              },
              {
                "text": "他说中文说得很好。",
                "pinyin": "tā shuō Zhōngwén shuō de hěn hǎo 。",
                "meaning": "He speaks Chinese well.",
